For every ordinary fourfold link over $Q$ one has $$\begin{aligned}
\label{sl:vertical-cocycle}
 c_{u,\mathrm{vert}/Q}(f)&=v(V'/Q)-v(V/Q),\\
\label{sl:horizontal-residual}
 c_u(f)-\bigl(v(V'/B')-v(V/B)\bigr)
 &=c_{u,\mathrm{hor}/Q}(f)-h_Q(V'/B')+h_Q(V/B).
\end{aligned}$$ These identities hold for every test degree and require no boundedness threshold.

outputs.exact_statement:
The sums in <a href="#pre:cocycle-definition" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="pre:cocycle-definition">[pre:cocycle-definition]</a> are finite. For birational maps $f:X\dashrightarrow Y$ and $g:Y\dashrightarrow Z$ of normal projective varieties, $$\label{pre:cocycle-additivity}
 c_u(g\circ f)=c_u(f)+c_u(g),\qquad
 c_u(f^{-1})=-c_u(f).$$ An isomorphism in codimension one has value zero. If $\pi:\widetilde X\to X$ is the blow-up of a smooth projective variety along a smooth center with connected components $Z_i$ of codimension at least two, then $$\label{pre:blowup-sign}
 c_u(\pi^{-1})=\sum_i u(Z_i),\qquad
 c_u(\pi)=-\sum_i u(Z_i).$$

For every ordinary fourfold link over $Q$ one has $$\begin{aligned}
\label{sl:vertical-cocycle}
 c_{u,\mathrm{vert}/Q}(f)&=v(V'/Q)-v(V/Q),\\
\label{sl:horizontal-residual}
 c_u(f)-\bigl(v(V'/B')-v(V/B)\bigr)
 &=c_{u,\mathrm{hor}/Q}(f)-h_Q(V'/B')+h_Q(V/B).
\end{aligned}$$ These identities hold for every test degree and require no boundedness threshold.
